  "body": "**Wanted:** a bundled starter library of common hobby-router bits with their stated reach (flute length, stick-out). It includes 1/8\" and 1/4\" (3 and 6 mm) up-cut, down-cut and compression end mills, 60 and 90 degree V-bits (with the flat-tip question of #895), 1/8\" and 1/4\" ball nose, and a spoilboard surfacing bit. Tools are generic and unbranded, with conservative wood cutting data once the wood materials issue lands. Branded libraries live in the separate community repo (mkinney/cam-tools-and-fixtures).\n\n**Done means:** a new user on a router machine can pick these from the tool library with no setup, and each imports cleanly (`import_tool_library` refuses nothing), pinned by a test.\n\nAsked by the user (mkinney), 2026-11-20, for hobby router owners (MisterMaker's WorkBee #3038, Mark's router #1907): \"Mark will prob want him for his router, too. So, it is not a let's wait until later issue; the sooner the better, within reason ofc\".\n\nPart of #3066 (findings: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/3066#issuecomment-7050655107). The clean-room boundary of #3066 applies: no vendor wording, labels, parameter names or dialog flows.",
